aved, and handwritten values refer to music fonts; the rest refer to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text fonts. The fantasy style refers to decorative text such as found in older German-style printing."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont/Size-swift.enum":{"title":"MXLFont.Size","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Size"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont\/size-swift.enum","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Size"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont\/Size-swift.enum","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font-size can be one of the CSS font sizes (xx-small, x-small, small, medium, large, x-large, xx-large) or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a numeric point size."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont/Weight-swift.enum":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLFont.Weight","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont\/Weight-swift.enum","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font-weight type represents a simplified version of the CSS font-weight property."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Weight"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Weight"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont\/weight-swift.enum"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont/Style-swift.enum":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLFont.Style","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont\/Style-swift.enum","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font-style type represents a simplified version of the CSS font-style property."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont\/style-swift.enum"}}}